.TH JRNL 1 "2026-10-10" "jrnlc 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
jrnl \- small plain-text command-line journal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jrnl
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ text ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B jrnl
stores entries in the plain-text format used by Python jrnl:
.PP
.nf
[YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM] entry text @tag
.fi
.PP
With no search option, positional text is appended as a new entry. If no text
is supplied, input is read from standard input.
.SH ADDING ENTRIES
.TP
.BI "jrnl " "text ..."
Add an entry using the current local time.
.TP
.BI "jrnl --date " "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM text ..."
Add an entry with an explicit timestamp.
.TP
.BI "jrnl --daily --journal-dir " "DIR text ..."
Add to the file named
.I journal-YYYY-MM-DD
in
.I DIR.
.SH SEARCH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "-n " N
Show the last
.I N
matching entries.
.TP
.BI "-contains " TERM
Match entry text. May be repeated.
.TP
.BI @TAG
Match entries containing the tag.
.TP
.BR -and
Require all positive selectors to match.
.TP
.BR -not
Negate the following selector.
.TP
.BR -starred
Match entries whose first line ends in an asterisk.
.TP
.BI "-from " DATE
Use an inclusive lower date bound.
.TP
.BI "-to " DATE
Use an inclusive upper date bound.
.TP
.BI "-until " DATE
Alias for
.BR -to .
.TP
.BI "-on " DATE
Match entries on one date, or one whole month when
.I DATE
is written as
.IR "Month YYYY" .
.PP
Dates may be written as
.I YYYY-MM-DD
or
.IR "Month YYYY" .
.SH OUTPUT
.TP
.BI "--format " FORMAT
Use
.BR pretty ,
.BR short ,
or
.BR json
output.
.TP
.BI "--export " FORMAT
Export matching entries as
.BR text
or
.BR json .
.TP
.B --tags
List unique tags.
.SH JOURNAL SELECTION
.TP
.BI "--journal " PATH
Read or write one explicit journal file.
.TP
.B --local
Use
.I .jrnlc/journal.txt.
.TP
.B --global
Use the global journal.
.TP
.B --daily
Read or write date-suffixed journal files in the selected directory.
.TP
.BI "--journal-dir " DIR
Use
.I DIR
for daily journal files. Files are named
.I journal-YYYY-MM-DD
and are read in lexical order.
.PP
Without an explicit selection, an existing local journal is preferred. Otherwise
the global journal is used. The global path is
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/jrnl/journal.txt
or, when XDG_DATA_HOME is unset,
.I $HOME/.local/share/jrnl/journal.txt.
.B JRNL_FILE
may override the default global path.
.SH OTHER OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Show usage.
.TP
.B --version
Show version.
.SH FILE SAFETY
New entries are written through a sibling temporary file. The existing file is
copied byte-for-byte, the new entry is appended, the temporary file is flushed
and synchronized, and it is atomically replaced over the original. This keeps
malformed or manually-added bytes intact and prevents readers from seeing a
partially-written replacement.
.PP
The program assumes a single writer. Atomic replacement does not coordinate
concurrent writers.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B JRNL_FILE
Override the default global journal path.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Set the base directory for the global journal.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Natural-language date parsing, encryption, editor integration, deletion, and
the complete Python jrnl configuration format are intentionally outside the
program. Use an external date helper or GPG when needed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
jrnl "finished the build" @work
jrnl -from 2025-01-01 -to 2025-01-31
jrnl -contains build -and @work
jrnl --daily --journal-dir ~/.jrnl "daily note"
jrnl --export json > journal.json
.fi
